# modbusspec-sweep 0: requests to a real device in the order sent, and their replies
device: inverter/goodwe/et
product: GoodWe ET, GW29.9K-ET (ARM firmware 04062-13-S00), 8 battery clusters
unit: 247
link: Modbus TCP, port 502, from a tablet on the site's LAN
date: 2026-10-28, 09:54:24 to 10:00:12 (+01:00); stopped in the function 04 pass after the connection failed twice
tool: 'AmslerSolarDashboard 0.6.3 (32) register sweep, read only (functions 03, 04): known registers only; its passes are the comment lines below; it waits about
  1000 ms for a reply'
masked: 'digits of serial numbers (inverter at 2000, 35003, 45203, 60052; battery modules at 22000, 22021, 22042, 22063, 22084, 22105, 22126, 22147,
  37060; another at 33943) as #; their letters are kept'
format: 'function address+count[*runs] reply. A run of n requests: each starting where the one before ended, same count, same reply. Reply: E code for an
  exception, S for no reply (a request sent again after it is a line of its own), or the words in hex, w*n for n equal words, M and two characters for
  a masked word (# a hidden digit).'
